# Generate complex sql query
思路：使用llm生成sql中部分内容使之复杂化，后拼接

This directory is placed inside LLM-R2/src

Currently there are two ways to make the query more
complicated. 1) Make the deepest subquery even deeper,
and 2) Make the WHERE clause more complicated.

Usage:
+ Run generator.py, specifiying the input(-i)
  and output(-o, default is ./) paths and the 
  method(-m) to make the query more complex.
  (example: python3 generator.py -i ../../data/data_llmr2/queries/queries_tpch_test.csv -m "deepest_query_multiple")

+ Add a new pipeline by adding a list containing all 
  the instructions in run_pipeline. If the pipeline 
  only needs to be run once, then nothing needs to be done.
  Otherwise, you might want to add some code to identify
  this method and handle it.

Supported methods:
+ deepest_query_once:
	+ Rewrite the deepest subquery of the input query, if 
	  the input query has no subqueries, returns the input
	  query.
+ deepest_query_multiple:
	+ Iterate the deepest_query_once process multiple times.
	  the number of iterations is hard-coded into generator.py

TODO:
+ deepest_query_multiple will repeatedly process those queries
  that don't have subqueries, which is useless. 
+ If the rewritten subquery has syntax errors, this query will 
  be abandoned, which leads to significant data loss, especially
  during multiple iterations. Should add recovery method(for
  example, resending the query rewriting task to the LLM or
  asking LLM to fix the error).


